// Layer_Security — Security Layer (layer 9 of 9)
// Manual render: https://app.eraser.io > Diagram-as-code (cloud architecture).
//   Create a NEW canvas named "Layer_Security".
// Export the PNG to materials/reports/figures/Layer_Security.png
// Icons: product logos where available in docs.eraser.io/docs/icons (checked
//   2026-07-11): istio, trivy, minio, kubernetes; the rest use generic icons
//   (OpenBao and Valkey do not use the Vault/Redis logos, different fork brands).
// Connectors: <> for factually two-way relations (mutual mTLS, AdmissionReview
//   request-verdict, scan-write report CR); > for one-way flows.
// Reference: subsec:lapisan-keamanan (Section IV.3, sec:arsitektur-terintegrasi);
//   tool detail for the layer on row 9 of tab:layanan_industri, detailing the same
//   layer in Figure fig:integrate-service (Section IV.1, without tools).
//   Included in LaTeX as fig:layer-security.
// Focus: identity (Dex OIDC, oauth2-proxy, SpiceDB), secrets (OpenBao + External
//   Secrets Operator), the edge (APISIX gateway) and the mTLS mesh (Istio), policy
//   and detection (Kyverno admission, Falco runtime, Trivy Operator scanning, Chaos
//   Mesh resilience testing), plus recovery (Velero backup to MinIO).
// Rendering MUST be horizontal (direction right): subgroups placed side by side, at most
//   two node rows per group, so the diagram spreads wide and fits the band
//   height=0.42\textheight. Included without \rotatebox in LaTeX.
// Layer grounding: the group label carries its source category, namely the security side
//   of the infrastructure and supporting services category (najafabadi2024analysis)
//   together with controlled access and data privacy and security compliance in the
//   DataOps definition (munappy2020adhoc), matching row 9 of tab:layanan_industri.
// Implementation check: all nodes exist under platform/components/ (common/auth =
//   Dex + oauth2-proxy, storage/spicedb, security/openbao, security/external-secrets,
//   common/istio, security/apisix, security/kyverno, security/falco,
//   security/trivy-operator, security/chaos-mesh, security/velero). Chaos Mesh
//   was added from the security component group (previously in Infra_Control operations).

direction right

// Platform User (boundary)
Platform User [icon: users, color: gray, label: "Platform User (business, data, model)"]

// Security Layer
Security Layer [icon: shield, color: red, label: "Security Layer (controlled access + data privacy and security compliance)"] {
  Edge and Mesh [icon: network] {
    APISIX [icon: globe, label: "APISIX (edge API gateway)"]
    Istio [icon: istio, label: "Istio (mTLS mesh)"]
  }
  Identity and Authorization [icon: key] {
    Dex [icon: key, label: "Dex (OIDC SSO)"]
    oauth2-proxy [icon: user-check, label: "oauth2-proxy (console SSO)"]
    SpiceDB [icon: shield-check, label: "SpiceDB (relationship-based authorization)"]
  }
  Secret [icon: lock] {
    OpenBao [icon: lock, label: "OpenBao (secret vault)"]
    ESO [icon: refresh-cw, label: "External Secrets Operator"]
  }
  Policy and Detection [icon: check-circle] {
    Kyverno [icon: check-circle, label: "Kyverno (admission policy)"]
    Falco [icon: siren, label: "Falco (runtime detection)"]
    Trivy Operator [icon: trivy, label: "Trivy Operator (vulnerability scanning)"]
    Chaos Mesh [icon: zap, label: "Chaos Mesh (resilience testing)"]
  }
  Recovery [icon: archive] {
    Velero [icon: archive, label: "Velero (backup)"]
  }
}

// Cross-layer security boundary
Kubernetes [icon: kubernetes, color: gray, label: "Kubernetes (k3s)"]
Platform Workload [icon: layers, color: gray, label: "Platform Workload"]
MinIO [icon: minio, color: green, label: "MinIO (backup target)"]

// Identity and authorization flow
Platform User > APISIX: edge access
APISIX > Istio: ingress into the mesh
APISIX > Dex: OIDC auth delegation
Istio > oauth2-proxy: ext_authz
oauth2-proxy > Dex: OIDC
Dex > SpiceDB: identity for relationship check
Istio <> Platform Workload: service-to-service mTLS

// Secret flow
OpenBao > ESO: secret distribution
ESO > Platform Workload: synced secret

// Policy, detection, and recovery flow
Kubernetes <> Kyverno: admission webhook (request and verdict)
Kubernetes > Falco: runtime and audit events
Trivy Operator <> Kubernetes: image scan and report CR
Chaos Mesh > Kubernetes: fault injection
Platform Workload > Velero: backup source
Velero > MinIO: write backup to object storage
